{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1578606655,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1NDc3NDM2NzU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/4000","origin":"github"},"title":"travis: Adjust DATALAD_REPO_VERSION in light of auto-upgrades","message":"This issue is being split off from gh-2969, specifically this comment by @bpoldrack:\n\n\u003e Subsequently we should also change the Travis builds, so they don't suggest to test sth, they actually do not test.\n\n---\n\nThe .travis.yml in master sets `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION` to 5 and 6, but, with the minimum git-annex version on master (7.20190503), both of those will get auto-upgraded to the v7, the current default repo version.\n\nWe should still make sure that we have AnnexRepo tests for that cover the auto-upgrading (I think we already do), but I don't see any reason we need dedicated runs for different `DATALAD_REPO_VERSION` (which means we can drop two builds from the matrix).","files":null}]}